# VisionDev (browser MCP)

When the user needs **clicks, typing, login, navigation, forms, or verifying toasts/errors/URLs** on a real site (including **localhost**), use the **VisionDev** MCP tools.

## Setup (once per machine)

1. Install **VisionDev** from the [Visual Studio Marketplace](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=SanidhyaThakur.visiondev).
2. In Cursor: **VisionDev: Connect MCP (Cursor + VS Code Copilot)** — writes `.cursor/mcp.json` and `.vscode/mcp.json`.
3. Reload the window. Run **`npx playwright install chromium`** if needed.

## Tools

1. **vision_open** — open `url`, `device`: mobile | desktop.
2. **vision_observe** — refresh snapshot after DOM/route changes; **IDs change every time**.
3. **vision_act** — use **only** IDs from the latest snapshot.
4. **vision_wait** / **vision_assert** — async UI and checks.
5. **vision_close** — end session.

Do not invent CSS selectors. On **vision_act** error, **vision_observe** again and retry.
